#
# Exemptions for the estate Trusted-Base Reduction Policy scanner
# (hyperpolymath/standards scripts/check-trusted-base.sh, wired as the
# governance `trusted-base` job). Format: one path fragment per line; a line
# whose first non-space character is '#' is a comment.
#
# Rationale, using the mechanism the policy itself provides for this case —
# "test fixtures that exist to be detected by the scanner":
#
# tests/trusted-base-fixtures/ contains .agda files with real escape hatches in
# them ON PURPOSE. No agda invocation in this repository is ever pointed at them;
# they are not modules and are not typechecked. They exist so that
# scripts/check-agda-trusted-base.sh can be demonstrated to have teeth in both
# directions by tests/check-trusted-base-fixtures.sh — a file that mentions the
# banned words in comments must pass, and files that really violate the
# discipline must be flagged. A scanner that has never flagged anything has never
# been shown to flag anything.
#
# Deliberately NOT exempt: proofs/agda/ (the real development) and tests/reject/
# (the negative controls). Both are scanned by this repository's budget-zero gate
# and by the estate policy, and both contain zero markers.
tests/trusted-base-fixtures/
